e is to point out problems/solutions with bootstrap script usage introduced in 1.7.3. With a fresh install of vagrant 1.7.4 (host: Trusty64), #5936 does not fix issues seemingly introduced with #5435.\n### Problems\n1. We need a clear and consistent way of customizing the arguments passed to the bootstrap script. This was the reason why @timoguin created #5435. The [documentation surrounding `install_args` and `bootstrap_options`](https://docs.vagrantup.com/v2/provisioning/salt.html) should properly reflect the  ~~quirks~~ behaviour of saltstack's bootstrap script.\n   - `bootstrap_options` applies to the flagged options passed the the bootstrap script that are required to appear first.\n   - `install_args` are for arguments such as branch name and install type (e.g. stable, git)\n2. The quickest way back to a _working_ state would be to revert **both** #5936 and #5435. \n3. We need [testing around `install_args` and `bootstrap_options` anyways](https://github.com/mitchellh/vagrant/blob/master/test/unit/plugins/provisioners/salt/config_test.rb)\n\nI'm working on all 3. PR soon.\n\nThoughts? @timoguin @mitchellh @cachedout @thatch45\n","closed_by":{"login":"chrisroberts","id":266674,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NjY3NA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266674?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisroberts","html_url":"https://github.com/chrisroberts","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisroberts/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisroberts/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisroberts/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisroberts/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisroberts/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisroberts/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisroberts/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/chrisroberts/events{/privacy}"